Tally was an old [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] deep in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], and the town that grew up around it. The heart was warm and cased in a metal shell, and buildings were raised in the heat that came off it. It was the strider's timekeeper: it kept the religious rites, logged what the strider did and where it went, and kept it moving smoothly forward. The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]] said it was already dead, and so it was: the heart had gone cold, its veins still. [[People/Galzu|Galzu]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]]'s sister, worked a rite to call it back and failed.

The heart is gone. The Machine God consumed it, and what was left blackened and fell to ash. The town remains.

The town around the heart is Neweth, old and buried in the strider. Its people, one to two thousand of them, are [[Bestiary/Mongrel Folk|mongrel folk]] and other outcasts indentured to the strider's owners. They trade in ration slips instead of coin and have built a working, somewhat violent civilization in the dark. They are unlikely to attack strangers on sight, though what they make of people outside their class is hard to guess. The remaining followers of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] on the strider, called the Herald's Children, keep to the town and pass for townsfolk, and people of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] have gone underground almost directly above it.
